# Drafted by Gemini (R17 rooms2c), edited.

~ l23_journal
Narrator: Shelves of pale specimens line Doctor Belkin's study, smelling sharply of vinegar and cold brine. Beside a jar of sleeping white grubs lies a thick leather ledger titled the Anatomist's Journal.
* [Arcana DC 14] Read the journal -> l23_journal_ok | l23_journal_fail
* [if not flag.mr_swarm_done] Open the larvae jar -> l23_swarm
* Leave -> END

~ l23_journal_ok
Narrator: Beneath Belkin's cramped diagrams of a great chained worm in a flooded grotto, {name} deciphers a phrase in the wet, clicking script of the deep-lake folk: the words that unseal a hidden hatch in the recovery ward.
give mr_belkin_journal
set mr_hatch_words
set mr_hatch_hint
set mr_truth_clues += 1
if flag.mr_truth_clues >= 2 and (quest.all_is_well == find_the_cousin or quest.all_is_well == sign_in)
if not quest.all_is_well >= the_truth
quest all_is_well the_truth
endif
endif
-> l23_journal

~ l23_journal_fail
Narrator: The pages are a tangle of cramped anatomical ciphers and strange aquatic script that refuses to yield its meaning.
-> l23_journal

~ l23_swarm
Narrator: The glass stopper comes free with a sour hiss, and the pale grubs wake all at once, boiling over the rim in a hungry tide.
combat mr_swarm

~ l24_pods
Narrator: The unlit room is clammy as a cellar, lined with six tall cradles of weeping grey membrane. Three of the pods hold sleeping surgeons, their chests rising slow and heavy beneath the slime.
* Touch a pod's gel -> l24_gel
* [if not flag.mr_swarm_done] Search an empty pod -> l24_search
* Leave -> END

~ l24_gel
Narrator: The cold jelly numbs {name}'s fingertips, and for ten breathless minutes another sight crowds in: a vast blind worm in chains far below, looking out through a hundred wet eyes in a dark cavern.
set mr_worm_seen
-> END

~ l24_search
Narrator: {name} parts the slick husk of an empty cradle, disturbing a knot of pale grubs coiled in the warmth at the bottom.
combat mr_swarm

~ l25_glass
Narrator: Through the observation glass, one tiled cell stands empty save for a warning scratched into the grout: DO NOT LET IT IN YOUR HEAD. In the next, a shivering patient clutches their open crown, where pale shapes stir.
mr_glass_patient [afraid]: Make them be still, please, they are whispering so loudly...
* [Medicine DC 15] Treat them with psychic harm to the worms -> l25_saved | l25_fail
* [if flag.lethic_antidote_doses >= 1] Draw the worms out with serum -> l25_saved
* Leave -> END

~ l25_saved
Narrator: The parasites shrivel and drop away from the wound, leaving the poor soul blinking in the violet gloom.
mr_glass_patient [weary]: It is quiet now, thank you. I cannot recall my name, only Doctor Belkin speaking strange words to a secret door in the recovery room...
set l25_patient_fate = "saved"
set mr_patients_saved += 1
set mr_hatch_hint
-> END

~ l25_fail
Narrator: The brood flinches deeper into the bone at {name}'s touch, and the patient's eyes glaze over with a cold, hollow calm.
mr_glass_patient [neutral]: We hear the choir beneath the stone now. You may leave us.
set l25_patient_fate = "lost"
-> END

~ l27_eye
Narrator: The corridor ends at a smooth plaster wall painted with a white barn owl perched in the boughs of a weeping willow.
* [Perception DC 16] Search the mural -> l27_eye_found | l27_eye_miss
* [if item:mr_lethic_serum and (flag.mr_lab_open_known or flag.mr_eye_found)] Inject the owl's eye with a full dose of serum -> l27_open
* Leave -> END

~ l27_eye_found
set mr_eye_found
Narrator: Looking close at the painted feathers, {name} spots a tiny brass-ringed aperture in the owl's left eye, crusted with dried violet serum.
-> l27_eye

~ l27_eye_miss
Narrator: The brushwork is fine and cold to the touch, showing nothing more than paint on seamless plaster.
-> END

~ l27_open
Narrator: The needle clicks home into the brass ring; as the serum drains inside, hidden counterweights groan and the painted wall swings open.
take mr_lethic_serum
set mr_lab_open
move mr_upper:from_lab

~ l27_lab
Narrator: Glass coils and brass tubing bubble with violet distillation across the worktables, filling the room with a sweet, numbing vapour. At the far end stand a crackling glass orb and a broad iron lift platform over a dark shaft.
* Search the alchemical chaos -> l27_search
* Take the unrefined ichor decanters -> l27_ichor
* Use the foot lever to the Widow's Wile -> l27_wile
* Ride the Plunge Platform down -> l27_platform
* Leave -> END

~ l27_search
Narrator: Among the warm retorts and notes, {name} finds a stoppered vial of refined violet serum ready for the needle.
give mr_lethic_serum
-> l27_lab

~ l27_ichor
Narrator: Heavy glass decanters sit in a rack of crushed ice, thick with milky, unrefined ichor drawn fresh from below.
if not flag.mr_ichor_taken
set mr_ichor_taken
set unrefined_ichor += 6
endif
-> l27_lab

~ l27_wile
Narrator: Wires trail from the mounted glass orb down into the shadow beneath the iron workbench.
* [Investigation DC 16] Find the foot lever -> l27_wile_ok | l27_lab
* Step back -> l27_lab

~ l27_wile_ok
Narrator: {name}'s boot finds a recessed brass pedal; the glass orb splits the air with purple lightning, and the floor vanishes in a roar of ozone and cold lake water.
set mr_wile_used
if not flag.mr_grotto_seen
if not quest.all_is_well >= the_way_down
quest all_is_well the_way_down
endif
endif
move mr_grotto:from_wile

~ l27_platform
Narrator: Chains clank and the iron platform lurches downward, sinking into the pitch-dark shaft toward the sound of lapping water.
if not flag.mr_grotto_seen
if not quest.all_is_well >= the_way_down
quest all_is_well the_way_down
endif
endif
move mr_grotto:from_lift
